proof.text:
Finally restrict three charts $a,a',a''$ to the triple overlap, inverting the two overlap ratios in each chart. Step 3 applies successively; step 4 preserves the ideals at each restriction. Write $q_a$ for the surjection from the resulting ordinary overlap ring to its torsion quotient. The ordinary cocycle of step 2, supplied by [lemma-nagata-proj-chart-ring-cocycle], gives
$$(\bar\theta_{a'a''}\bar\theta_{aa'})q_a
=q_{a''}\theta_{a'a''}\theta_{aa'}
=q_{a''}\theta_{aa''}
=\bar\theta_{aa''}q_a.$$
Every element of the source quotient is $q_a(w)$, so this is the asserted triple cocycle. Localizing this equation further preserves it: every fraction maps to the image of its numerator times the inverse image of its denominator. The double-localization equality of step 1 and the comparison squares of step 5 identify these maps with the localized strict-transform chart comparisons, in either order of restriction. The choices $a,a',a''$ and the further localizations were arbitrary, so this proves both clauses of the item.
